What is India High end Copper Foil?
India High end Copper Foil refers to copper conductor that meets stringent specifications for thickness, surface roughness and purity, produced by Indian manufacturers for high value end uses. Thickness typically ranges from 6 µm to 35 µm, with the most sought after grades falling below 9 µm for advanced battery and telecom applications. Surface roughness is kept under 0.5 µm to ensure low electrical resistance, while impurity levels are restricted to less than 10 ppm to protect cell chemistry and signal integrity.
The material is a cornerstone of two fast growing technology pillars: electric vehicle (EV) batteries, where copper content in lithium ion cells has risen to roughly 12 15 % by weight, and 5G telecommunications, which depend on Very Low Profile (VLP) and Hyper Very Low Profile (HVLP) foils to minimise insertion loss at millimetre wave frequencies. Production involves electrolytic deposition, precision rolling and, increasingly, nano coating processes that enhance oxidation resistance and conductivity.
